<% content_for :title, "Introduction — Shadwire" %>
<% content_for :description, "shadcn/ui for Ruby on Rails: ViewComponent components whose source you install in your app and then maintain as your own." %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= tag.style rouge_stylesheet %>
<% end %>

<article class="space-y-12">
  <%= render "docs/header",
        title: "Introduction",
        description: "shadcn/ui for Ruby on Rails. The CLI copies each component's source into your app, and from then on the code is yours." %>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <p class="leading-7">
      shadcn/ui changed the usual deal with a UI library. Instead of installing a package and
      configuring it from the outside, you copy each component's source into your project and
      edit it like the rest of your code. Shadwire does the same for Rails. The components are
      <%= link_to "ViewComponent", "https://viewcomponent.org", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>
      classes styled with Tailwind CSS v4, and a CLI installs them from a static registry.
    </p>

    <%= render layout: "docs/callout", locals: { icon: "info", title: "No runtime dependency" } do %>
      The <code>shadwire</code> gem goes in the <code>development</code> group and is only used
      to install and update files. If you remove it, the installed components keep working.
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("How it works") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      A component gets from the registry into your app in three steps.
    </p>

    <ol class="space-y-4">
      <% [
        { step: "1", title: "The registry publishes",
          body: "Each component is published at https://shadwire.edumoraes.dev.br/r as a JSON file that carries the contents of its source files. They are plain static files: there is no application server and no login." },
        { step: "2", title: "The CLI installs",
          body: "bin/shadwire add button fetches the item, writes the files to their paths in your app, adds the gems and importmap pins it needs, and records all of it in shadwire.json." },
        { step: "3", title: "You own it",
          body: "From then on the files are part of your app. Change variants, classes or names as you see fit; bin/shadwire diff shows what you changed compared to the registry." }
      ].each do |item| %>
        <li class="flex gap-4">
          <span class="flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary/10 text-sm font-semibold text-primary">
            <%= item[:step] %>
          </span>
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <p class="font-medium"><%= item[:title] %></p>
            <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground"><%= item[:body] %></p>
          </div>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>

    <%= docs_code_block(<<~SHELL, language: :shell) %>
      gem install shadwire
      shadwire init                     # shadwire.json + base files + bin/shadwire
      bin/shadwire add button card      # installs components and their dependencies
    SHELL
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-6">
    <%= docs_h2("Principles") %>

    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <% [
        { icon: "package-open", title: "Open Code",
          body: "The component's code sits in your repository, where you can read and change it. When a component does not cover your case, you edit the file instead of hunting for a configuration option." },
        { icon: "blocks", title: "Composition",
          body: "You build a component out of nested helpers rather than props: ui_card_header goes inside ui_card, ui_select_item inside ui_select_content. The view reads like the HTML it produces." },
        { icon: "palette", title: "Semantic tokens",
          body: "Colours come from shadcn's tokens (bg-primary, text-muted-foreground). To change the theme you edit two lists of CSS variables, one for light and one for dark, and leave the components alone." },
        { icon: "accessibility", title: "Accessible by default",
          body: "The components follow the WAI-ARIA APG patterns for focus, keyboard use, labels and states, and the test suite checks this on every change." },
        { icon: "bot", title: "Ready for agents",
          body: "An agent skill and the llms.txt files describe the catalog in plain text, and every CLI command accepts --json, so a coding agent can look up a component's API instead of guessing it." },
        { icon: "git-compare-arrows", title: "Explicit updates",
          body: "Installed files only change when you ask. diff shows how your copy differs from the registry, and update brings in the registry's version and tells you what it overwrote." }
      ].each do |principle| %>
        <%= ui_card(class: "h-full") do %>
          <%= ui_card_header do %>
            <%= ui_card_title(class: "flex items-center gap-2 text-base") do %>
              <%= ui_icon(principle[:icon], class: "text-primary") %><%= principle[:title] %>
            <% end %>
            <%= ui_card_description(class: "leading-6") { principle[:body] } %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("What's available") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      <%= docs_component_items.size %> components and 1 block, each one tested in the Rails app
      that serves this site.
    </p>

    <%= render "docs/table",
          headers: [ "Area", "Components" ],
          rows: [
            [ "Forms", docs_code("field") + " · " + docs_code("input") + " · " + docs_code("textarea") + " · " + docs_code("checkbox") + " · " + docs_code("radio-group") + " · " + docs_code("switch") + " · " + docs_code("select") + " · " + docs_code("combobox") + " · " + docs_code("slider") + " · " + docs_code("input-otp") + " · " + docs_code("date-picker") ],
            [ "Overlays", docs_code("dialog") + " · " + docs_code("alert-dialog") + " · " + docs_code("sheet") + " · " + docs_code("drawer") + " · " + docs_code("popover") + " · " + docs_code("tooltip") + " · " + docs_code("hover-card") ],
            [ "Navigation", docs_code("sidebar") + " · " + docs_code("navigation-menu") + " · " + docs_code("menubar") + " · " + docs_code("breadcrumb") + " · " + docs_code("tabs") + " · " + docs_code("pagination") + " · " + docs_code("command") ],
            [ "Data", docs_code("table") + " · " + docs_code("data-table") + " · " + docs_code("chart") + " · " + docs_code("card") + " · " + docs_code("item") + " · " + docs_code("badge") + " · " + docs_code("avatar") ],
            [ "State", docs_code("skeleton") + " · " + docs_code("spinner") + " · " + docs_code("progress") + " · " + docs_code("empty") + " · " + docs_code("alert") + " · " + docs_code("sonner") ]
          ] %>

    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      The full catalog is on the <%= link_to "Components", components_path, class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>
      page, and <%= docs_code("bin/shadwire list") %> prints the same list.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Where to start") %>
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <% [
        { icon: "download", title: "Installation", body: "Requirements, the CLI, and your first component in your app.", path: docs_installation_path },
        { icon: "terminal", title: "CLI", body: "All the commands and flags, and the JSON output.", path: docs_cli_path },
        { icon: "palette", title: "Theming", body: "The colour tokens, your brand colour, and keeping your edits through updates.", path: docs_theming_path },
        { icon: "bot", title: "Agent skill", body: "What Claude Code, Codex and other agents need to know to use Shadwire.", path: docs_agent_skill_path }
      ].each do |card| %>
        <%= link_to card[:path], class: "group flex h-full flex-col gap-2 rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-card-foreground shadow-xs transition-colors hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] focus-visible:outline-none" do %>
          <span class="flex items-center gap-2 font-medium">
            <%= ui_icon(card[:icon], size: :sm, class: "text-primary") %><%= card[:title] %>
          </span>
          <span class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground group-hover:text-accent-foreground"><%= card[:body] %></span>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <%= docs_h2("Licence") %>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Shadwire is MIT licensed. The components the CLI installs are yours: you can change them
      and ship them in commercial or closed-source products without adding attribution to the
      installed files.
    </p>
    <p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
      Shadwire is a port of
      <%= link_to "shadcn/ui", "https://ui.shadcn.com", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>,
      which is also MIT licensed. Its licence notice, and those of the libraries the components
      use (view_component, lucide-rails, the Lucide icons, D3), are in the repository's
      <%= link_to "NOTICE", "https://github.com/edumoraes/shadwire/blob/main/NOTICE", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: "font-medium underline underline-offset-4" %>.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
